{"level":30,"time":1778270823411,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019R84h5J3G9m8T14zD3MSdX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"From what I can see:\n- Sheet 9 (site plan) shows detailed layouts with buildings, parking, utilities, etc. It mentions \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date\" but I need to check if there are overhead electric lines shown\n- Sheet 35 (landscape calculations) lists trees including Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud, shrubs, and groundcovers\n- The landscape plan does mention \"overhead electric (OHE)\" in Block 2 of Sheet 31\n\nNow I need to actually look at the vision content to see if there are overhead electric lines shown on the site plans. Let me check the site plan guide summaries first to understand what's actually depicted.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8474,"cache_read_input_tokens":46093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8474},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7795528a-4d8c-4fde-927d-805a3b7ab056","uuid":"ac2d28d5-6559-4f84-a51c-35cc6cf52a25"}
{"level":30,"time":1778270823515,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NFQMR2gdveXAG3RsZCoPJQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good data now. From the blocks I can see:\n\n**Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan):**\n- Shows utility lines including \"overhead electric (OHE)\" marked on the plan\n- Shows buildings and parking areas\n- Shows trees and vegetation indicated by symbols\n- Key notes define symbols for trees: SY (street yard tree), PL (parking lot tree), P (parking buffer point tree), M (mitigation tree)\n- However, the blocks don't specify details about:\n  - Which specific tree species are proposed\n  - Where exactly overhead electric lines are in relation to trees\n  - Any clearance measurements\n  - Any reference to utility compatibility\n\n**Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan):**\n- Shows underground electric lines, transformers, pull boxes, electrical meters\n- References \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list\" - but sheet 32 is the tree list, not the plant schedule\n- No mention of overhead electric lines on this sheet - it's focused on underground electrical design\n- NOTE: The guide says \"Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\" shows overhead electric, but Sheet 21 (Electrical Design) shows underground electric infrastructure\n\n**Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations & Plant Lists):**\n- Lists shade trees: 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.)\n- Lists ornamental trees: 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.)\n- Lists shrubs and groundcovers\n- NO mention of utility compatibility (UC designation from ECM Appendix F)\n- NO mention of mature heights for the trees\n- NO specific notation that these are utility-compatible or not\n\nKey findings so far:\n1. The site DOES have overhead electric lines marked on the landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n2. The site DOES have proposed trees (12 shade trees total, 8 ornamental trees, plus shrubs)\n\n\n3. The plant schedule omits utility compatibility designations and mature heights—both critical for assessing compliance with EL-2.1 through EL-2.4. Without these details, I can't determine if the species meet utility-compatible requirements or if any reach the 40+ foot threshold that triggers additional restrictions. The overhead electric lines are marked on the landscape plan, but there's no documentation showing clearance distances or compatibility checks between the proposed trees and those utilities.\n\nI need to examine the landscape drawing directly to see how the overhead lines are positioned relative to the tree locations and assess whether the design adequately addresses the clearance and compatibility standards.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7658,"cache_read_input_tokens":41385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7658},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"9735a57f-db38-40fe-99e2-17be88ad14f9"}
