{"level":30,"time":1778270868992,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NehANndHfmQKBFYAqE8x3n","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Master Comment Report\n     2→\n     3→A comprehensive compilation of city staff review comments requiring updates for a site plan application.\n     4→\n     5→## Sections\n     6→\n     7→1. **General Information and Case Manager Review** (pp. 1-2)\n     8→   Provides project details, update deadlines, submittal requirements, and the case manager's initial site plan comments.\n     9→   File: `01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md`\n    10→2. **Electric Review** (pp. 2-3)\n    11→   Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.\n    12→   File: `02-electric-review.md`\n    13→3. **Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review** (pp. 3-9)\n    14→   Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.\n    15→   File: `03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md`\n    16→4. **Drainage Engineering Review** (pp. 9-14)\n    17→   Reviews the project's storm water management, drainage easements, retaining walls, dam safety, and DCM waiver requirements.\n    18→   File: `04-drainage-engineering-review.md`\n    19→5. **Environmental Review** (p. 14)\n    20→   Details pending requirements for environmental and landscape inspection fees and ESC fiscal surety.\n    21→   File: `05-environmental-review.md`\n    22→6. **Fire For Site Plan Review** (pp. 14-15)\n    23→   Outlines fire department requirements regarding general notes, access roads, and fire hydrant flow constraints.\n    24→   File: `06-fire-for-site-plan-review.md`\n    25→7. **Land Development Engineering** (p. 15)\n    26→   Identifies items needing a License Agreement and requires adjustments to a driveway detail.\n    27→   File: `07-land-development-engineering.md`\n    28→8. **PARD / Planning & Design Review** (pp. 15-16)\n    29→   Details the pending parkland dedication fee amount required prior to the issuance of the certificate of occupancy.\n    30→   File: `08-pard-planning-design-review.md`\n    31→9. **Site Plan Review** (pp. 16-17)\n    32→   Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.\n    33→   File: `09-site-plan-review.md`\n    34→10. **Site Plan Plumbing Review** (pp. 17-18)\n    35→   Reviews the required drainage fixture unit loading and asks for pipe sizing, slopes, and materials to be documented.\n    36→   File: `10-site-plan-plumbing-review.md`\n    37→11. **AW Utility Development Services** (p. 18)\n    38→   Notes that the site is in an area of capacity concern and requires a Service Extension Request for wastewater.\n    39→   File: `11-aw-utility-development-services.md`\n    40→12. **Water Quality Review** (pp. 18-21)\n    41→   Assesses water quality controls, impervious cover treatment, pond design dimensions, and biofiltration compliance.\n    42→   File: `12-water-quality-review.md`\n    43→13. **AW Pipeline Engineering** (p. 21)\n    44→   Provides a link to download redline review comments for the pipeline engineering portion.\n    45→   File: `13-aw-pipeline-engineering.md`\n    46→14. **City Arborist Review** (pp. 21-25)\n    47→   Specifies tree preservation criteria, variance requirements for heritage trees, and mitigation procedures.\n    48→   File: `14-city-arborist-review.md`\n    49→15. **AW OWB Review & Comment Resolution** (pp. 26-27)\n    50→   Reviews building coverage and gross floor area reporting constraints and outlines the comment resolution process.\n    51→   File: `15-aw-owb-review-comment-resolution.md`\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb743e7b-dade-42fe-a871-055cf9865568","uuid":"70cd77ea-fee5-4b83-9981-55e4559ac4cb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/overview.md","content":"# Master Comment Report\n\nA comprehensive compilation of city staff review comments requiring updates for a site plan application.\n\n## Sections\n\n1. **General Information and Case Manager Review** (pp. 1-2)\n   Provides project details, update deadlines, submittal requirements, and the case manager's initial site plan comments.\n   File: `01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md`\n2. **Electric Review** (pp. 2-3)\n   Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.\n   File: `02-electric-review.md`\n3. **Transportation & Public Works (TPW-TDS) Review** (pp. 3-9)\n   Details requirements related to parking, street impact fees, right-of-way, driveways, and trash collection.\n   File: `03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md`\n4. **Drainage Engineering Review** (pp. 9-14)\n   Reviews the project's storm water management, drainage easements, retaining walls, dam safety, and DCM waiver requirements.\n   File: `04-drainage-engineering-review.md`\n5. **Environmental Review** (p. 14)\n   Details pending requirements for environmental and landscape inspection fees and ESC fiscal surety.\n   File: `05-environmental-review.md`\n6. **Fire For Site Plan Review** (pp. 14-15)\n   Outlines fire department requirements regarding general notes, access roads, and fire hydrant flow constraints.\n   File: `06-fire-for-site-plan-review.md`\n7. **Land Development Engineering** (p. 15)\n   Identifies items needing a License Agreement and requires adjustments to a driveway detail.\n   File: `07-land-development-engineering.md`\n8. **PARD / Planning & Design Review** (pp. 15-16)\n   Details the pending parkland dedication fee amount required prior to the issuance of the certificate of occupancy.\n   File: `08-pard-planning-design-review.md`\n9. **Site Plan Review** (pp. 16-17)\n   Requires updates to unit counts, site area calculations, building data tables, lighting notes, and administrative notes.\n   File: `09-site-plan-review.md`\n10. **Site Plan Plumbing Review** (pp. 17-18)\n   Reviews the required drainage fixture unit loading and asks for pipe sizing, slopes, and materials to be documented.\n   File: `10-site-plan-plumbing-review.md`\n11. **AW Utility Development Services** (p. 18)\n   Notes that the site is in an area of capacity concern and requires a Service Extension Request for wastewater.\n   File: `11-aw-utility-development-services.md`\n12. **Water Quality Review** (pp. 18-21)\n   Assesses water quality controls, impervious cover treatment, pond design dimensions, and biofiltration compliance.\n   File: `12-water-quality-review.md`\n13. **AW Pipeline Engineering** (p. 21)\n   Provides a link to download redline review comments for the pipeline engineering portion.\n   File: `13-aw-pipeline-engineering.md`\n14. **City Arborist Review** (pp. 21-25)\n   Specifies tree preservation criteria, variance requirements for heritage trees, and mitigation procedures.\n   File: `14-city-arborist-review.md`\n15. **AW OWB Review & Comment Resolution** (pp. 26-27)\n   Reviews building coverage and gross floor area reporting constraints and outlines the comment resolution process.\n   File: `15-aw-owb-review-comment-resolution.md`\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778270869000,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WFPnBxvYM56fww2yDkhWXG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - this is important. The trees near the overhead electric line on Sheet 31 are labeled with functional categories (M, PL, SY) but NOT with species. To identify the species, you need to cross-reference with the plant schedule.\n\nFrom what I found earlier on Sheet 35:\n- 2 Live Oak (100 gal.)\n- 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.)\n- Plus shrubs and groundcovers\n\nBut the plant schedule on Sheet 35 does NOT provide:\n- The mature heights of these trees\n- Whether they are utility-compatible (UC designation)\n- Which specific trees are placed where (the sheet shows quantities but not specific locations)\n\nSo to verify EL-2.10 (Plant legend does not identify species), I need to check if Sheet 31 actually provides a link to the plant schedule or if species are visible on Sheet 31. Let me check if there's a detailed plant legend/key notes block on Sheet 31 that identifies trees by species.\n\nActually, let me also look at whether the trees are labeled with dimensions (mature height) to identify if any are \"large trees\" (40+ feet).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":50407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"ce6a3f8f-e9aa-49df-bbf3-f8ade6af93f4"}
