{"level":30,"time":1778271133914,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0178QTU2JRYXgYsdZRvjAxmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - so there are NO clearance measurements shown on the landscape plan between trees and the overhead electric line. This is a significant finding.\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Whether any utility compatibility information is noted on the plans or in the plant schedule\n2. Whether there are any Austin Energy approvals mentioned\n3. Whether any trees are shown near utility poles or other electrical equipment\n\nLet me check what species are actually proposed. From Sheet 35, I see:\n- 2 Live Oak\n- 10 Cedar Elm  \n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n- 6 Mexican Redbud\n- 12 Dwarf Palmetto\n- 24 Big Muhly\n- 29 Gulf Muhly\n- 8 Texas Sage\n- 8 Dwarf Wax Myrtle\n\nI need to check ECM Appendix F to determine which of these are utility-compatible (UC) and which are 40+ feet mature height. But the plans themselves don't reference this information.\n\nLet me also check if there's any mention of pole-free zones (10 feet from poles) or other clearance issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":51814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"e5fc321a-1910-4551-ba36-90ba9a552c55"}
