{"level":30,"time":1778271146046,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtFpc4kxo36renKit88NNQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, there is a note addressing this requirement. \n\nUnder the **Electric Transmission Notes** section (located in the top-middle area of the sheet), Note #3 requires notifying Austin Energy 48 hours before starting construction to schedule a safety meeting regarding work near energized transmission lines. \n\nThe exact text is as follows:\n\n> \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\nAdditionally, under the **Electric Notes** section, Note #4 generally addresses the responsibility to maintain safe clearances near overhead lines:\n\n> \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\""}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7795528a-4d8c-4fde-927d-805a3b7ab056","uuid":"bff3ab06-beb8-4109-a441-cdf2d7472960","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, there is a note addressing this requirement. \n\nUnder the **Electric Transmission Notes** section (located in the top-middle area of the sheet), Note #3 requires notifying Austin Energy 48 hours before starting construction to schedule a safety meeting regarding work near energized transmission lines. \n\nThe exact text is as follows:\n\n> \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\nAdditionally, under the **Electric Notes** section, Note #4 generally addresses the responsibility to maintain safe clearances near overhead lines:\n\n> \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\""}]}
