{"level":30,"time":1778271524349,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjQCgHpNnfaqxPxciUyemU","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding the Overhead Electric (OHE) line and vehicular areas:\n\n**1. Driveways or Parking Areas Passing Under the OHE Line:**\n*   **Yes, there is a driveway passing under an OHE line.**\n*   Scanning the drawing, a linetype explicitly labeled with \"**--- OHE ---**\" runs along the bottom (southern) edge of the site plan, parallel to the property line.\n*   On the far left side of this southern boundary, the \"--- OHE ---\" line crosses directly over the main entrance driveway to the site.\n*   The driveway area it crosses is labeled exactly as:\n    \"**Construct Type III**\n    **Driveway**\n    **See Detail 433S-2**\"\n*   There are **no parking areas** shown passing under this or any other OHE line on this plan sheet. All depicted parking spaces are located further interior to the site.\n\n**2. Approximate Distances:**\n*   At the location where the OHE line crosses the driveway entrance, there is a dimension line indicating the width of the driveway.\n*   The driveway width passing under the line is dimensioned exactly as \"**29.0'**\".\n\n**3. Section Views and Vertical Clearance Dimensions:**\n*   **No section views** (such as profile cuts showing elevation) are indicated on this plan view near the OHE crossing.\n*   **No vertical clearance dimensions** (explicit height measurements from the pavement to the wires) are shown anywhere near the intersection of the driveway and the OHE line on this specific document. The reference \"See Detail 433S-2\" typically refers to a standard construction detail for the pavement apron, not an overhead utility profile."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7795528a-4d8c-4fde-927d-805a3b7ab056","uuid":"e867cee5-6588-44d0-9c69-288034575e83","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding the Overhead Electric (OHE) line and vehicular areas:\n\n**1. Driveways or Parking Areas Passing Under the OHE Line:**\n*   **Yes, there is a driveway passing under an OHE line.**\n*   Scanning the drawing, a linetype explicitly labeled with \"**--- OHE ---**\" runs along the bottom (southern) edge of the site plan, parallel to the property line.\n*   On the far left side of this southern boundary, the \"--- OHE ---\" line crosses directly over the main entrance driveway to the site.\n*   The driveway area it crosses is labeled exactly as:\n    \"**Construct Type III**\n    **Driveway**\n    **See Detail 433S-2**\"\n*   There are **no parking areas** shown passing under this or any other OHE line on this plan sheet. All depicted parking spaces are located further interior to the site.\n\n**2. Approximate Distances:**\n*   At the location where the OHE line crosses the driveway entrance, there is a dimension line indicating the width of the driveway.\n*   The driveway width passing under the line is dimensioned exactly as \"**29.0'**\".\n\n**3. Section Views and Vertical Clearance Dimensions:**\n*   **No section views** (such as profile cuts showing elevation) are indicated on this plan view near the OHE crossing.\n*   **No vertical clearance dimensions** (explicit height measurements from the pavement to the wires) are shown anywhere near the intersection of the driveway and the OHE line on this specific document. The reference \"See Detail 433S-2\" typically refers to a standard construction detail for the pavement apron, not an overhead utility profile."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778271524349,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NjKzjVT5eyiEQ9okGAkcRo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here are the answers to your questions, along with precise details extracted from the document.\n\n**1. Are there underground electric equipment locations (pull boxes, vaults, underground transformers) marked on the electrical design plan?**\n\n**Yes.** The plan extensively marks underground electrical lines (indicated by solid blue lines with an \"E\") and associated equipment using blue symbols connected to text callout boxes.\n\nThe following exact labels are used repeatedly across the plan to identify electrical equipment:\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** (pointing to small blue circles)\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (pointing to blue rectangles containing a diagonal line or cross)\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"** (pointing to small blue squares adjacent to buildings)\n\nAdditionally, there is a dashed rectangle labeled **\"Vault Easement\"** located on the west side of \"Bldg. 8\" (Unit 801), directly adjacent to an \"Electrical Meters\" location. A note in the center of the drawing, pointing to the main line running east-west, reads **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n\n**2. Are they positioned close to any of the tree locations shown on the landscape plan?**\n\n**Yes.** The base map includes topographical features, including large circles with scalloped/squiggly outlines representing tree canopies (drip lines). Several marked electrical equipment locations and their connecting underground lines are positioned very close to, or directly underneath, these tree canopies.\n\nHere are specific instances where electrical equipment is located in close proximity to trees:\n\n*   **South of Bldg. 7 / Bldg. 6:** Near the bottom center/right of the plan, adjacent to the southern property line, there is an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. The blue circle indicating this pull box is positioned directly inside the scalloped boundary of a large tree canopy.\n*   **West of Bldg. 8:** On the lower-left side of the plan, west of \"Unit 801\", there is an **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** and an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These are located immediately adjacent to the eastern edge of a large, dense cluster of tree canopies. Furthermore, the underground electric line running south from this equipment passes directly underneath the canopy of a tree located near the southwest corner of the property.\n*   **Northwest of Bldg. 1:** In the upper-left quadrant, north of \"Unit 101\", an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** is situated very close to the edge of a large tree canopy extending into the property from the north. The main underground line connecting to it runs through the outer edge of this canopy.\n*   **Northern Property Boundary:** The main underground electric line running along the northern edge of the property (north of Bldg. 1, 3, and 5) passes directly underneath or extremely close to the edges of several large tree canopies drawn along that boundary line.\n\n***\n\n**Transcription of Relevant Notes on the Plan:**\n\nFor complete accuracy regarding utilities, here is the exact transcription of the \"Utility Notes\" box located in the bottom right quadrant:\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"cd083f08-71aa-4fcc-9fae-1a61c29a008c","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here are the answers to your questions, along with precise details extracted from the document.\n\n**1. Are there underground electric equipment locations (pull boxes, vaults, underground transformers) marked on the electrical design plan?**\n\n**Yes.** The plan extensively marks underground electrical lines (indicated by solid blue lines with an \"E\") and associated equipment using blue symbols connected to text callout boxes.\n\nThe following exact labels are used repeatedly across the plan to identify electrical equipment:\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** (pointing to small blue circles)\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** (pointing to blue rectangles containing a diagonal line or cross)\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"** (pointing to small blue squares adjacent to buildings)\n\nAdditionally, there is a dashed rectangle labeled **\"Vault Easement\"** located on the west side of \"Bldg. 8\" (Unit 801), directly adjacent to an \"Electrical Meters\" location. A note in the center of the drawing, pointing to the main line running east-west, reads **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n\n**2. Are they positioned close to any of the tree locations shown on the landscape plan?**\n\n**Yes.** The base map includes topographical features, including large circles with scalloped/squiggly outlines representing tree canopies (drip lines). Several marked electrical equipment locations and their connecting underground lines are positioned very close to, or directly underneath, these tree canopies.\n\nHere are specific instances where electrical equipment is located in close proximity to trees:\n\n*   **South of Bldg. 7 / Bldg. 6:** Near the bottom center/right of the plan, adjacent to the southern property line, there is an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. The blue circle indicating this pull box is positioned directly inside the scalloped boundary of a large tree canopy.\n*   **West of Bldg. 8:** On the lower-left side of the plan, west of \"Unit 801\", there is an **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** and an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These are located immediately adjacent to the eastern edge of a large, dense cluster of tree canopies. Furthermore, the underground electric line running south from this equipment passes directly underneath the canopy of a tree located near the southwest corner of the property.\n*   **Northwest of Bldg. 1:** In the upper-left quadrant, north of \"Unit 101\", an **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** is situated very close to the edge of a large tree canopy extending into the property from the north. The main underground line connecting to it runs through the outer edge of this canopy.\n*   **Northern Property Boundary:** The main underground electric line running along the northern edge of the property (north of Bldg. 1, 3, and 5) passes directly underneath or extremely close to the edges of several large tree canopies drawn along that boundary line.\n\n***\n\n**Transcription of Relevant Notes on the Plan:**\n\nFor complete accuracy regarding utilities, here is the exact transcription of the \"Utility Notes\" box located in the bottom right quadrant:\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778271527103,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LQGzFRBwfSHLNDpEoevd4B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Critical finding: A driveway crosses under the OHE line on the south side (main entrance), but there are NO section views and NO vertical clearance dimensions shown to demonstrate that the 16 or 18-foot minimum vertical clearance is maintained. This is a clear deficiency under EL-1.18.\n\nAlso, per the grouping description, section/profile views are supposed to be provided by the applicant to show vertical relationships between overhead conductors and site features like driveways.\n\nNow let me check for any other site features that might be under the overhead line (such as decorative lighting, signage, trash enclosures, etc.).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":76489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":939},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7795528a-4d8c-4fde-927d-805a3b7ab056","uuid":"f4b7add0-3f50-4a43-bb0b-deb503cd81a6"}
