{"level":30,"time":1778271527352,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Xr39EfBJVekCeveu4ynuvf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important findings:\n\n**Tree distances to transformer pad (southwest corner):**\n- Tree immediately north: 10.2 feet (EXCEEDS the 10-foot minimum, but just barely - medium confidence)\n- Tree immediately south: 21.1 feet (complies)\n\nThe tree at 10.2 feet is essentially at the borderline. The requirement is \"within 10 lateral feet\" so 10.2 feet would technically comply if accurately measured. However, the medium confidence suggests this measurement may have some margin of error.\n\nBut more importantly, even if the distances technically comply, I still need to verify that the trees are identified as utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F. The vision tool didn't provide species identification.\n\nLet me check the tree list (Sheet 32) to see what species are planted where.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":63138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb743e7b-dade-42fe-a871-055cf9865568","uuid":"8da7ae6e-23ca-46f4-8fc0-611c48fa2980"}
