{"level":30,"time":1778271574980,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MiYSyUVavcVj26XQPtX3pG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan, here are the observations regarding customer facilities positioned near Overhead Electric (OHE) lines or electric easements:\n\n**1. Location of OHE Lines and Electric Easements:**\n*   **OHE Lines:** Lines explicitly labeled `---OHE---` run along the exterior of the western property boundary and along the southern property boundary.\n*   **Electric Easements:**\n    *   A **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is indicated by a dashed line running inside parallel to the southern property line.\n    *   A **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69 Pg. 14 Vol. 73 Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is labeled on the middle-eastern property boundary (east of Bldg. 6).\n    *   A **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is labeled near the bottom-right (southeast) corner.\n\n**2. Analysis of Facilities against OHE/Easement Locations:**\n\n*   **Buildings (Bldg. 1 - Bldg. 8):** None of the primary building structures appear to be positioned directly under the `---OHE---` lines or within the dashed boundaries of the labeled electric easements.\n*   **Trash Enclosures:** There are no distinct masonry trash enclosures or dumpster pads plotted on this plan (the \"Trash Collection Notes\" suggest the use of curbside containers rather than a fixed enclosure structure).\n*   **Lighting Fixtures:** Specific locations for light poles are not plotted on this plan (only a detail drawing for \"Fully-Shielded Light Fixtures\" is provided in the bottom left). Therefore, conflicts cannot be determined from this sheet.\n*   **Signs:** A \"Road End Sign\" is shown on the far left side, but it appears to be located in the public right-of-way outside the primary property boundary's OHE line. No other signs are explicitly plotted within easements on the site.\n*   **Structures (Retaining Walls, Flatwork):**\n    *   *Potential Conflict (Retaining Wall):* Along the middle-eastern property boundary, there is a label for a **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69 Pg. 14 Vol. 73 Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** Directly within this area, running parallel to the property line, is a solid line representing a wall. A leader line points directly to this wall with the exact text: **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**. Based on the drawing, this structure is positioned within the labeled electric easement.\n    *   *Flatwork Intersections:* While standard flatwork is not always classified as a structural \"facility\" depending on specific local utility codes, it should be noted that the elements labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway\"** (on both the western and southern boundaries) and **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\"** (on the western boundary) physically cross directly under/over the lines marked `---OHE---` to connect to the public roadway."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7795528a-4d8c-4fde-927d-805a3b7ab056","uuid":"68282670-1737-46bb-914f-a4104a6cd9cc","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan, here are the observations regarding customer facilities positioned near Overhead Electric (OHE) lines or electric easements:\n\n**1. Location of OHE Lines and Electric Easements:**\n*   **OHE Lines:** Lines explicitly labeled `---OHE---` run along the exterior of the western property boundary and along the southern property boundary.\n*   **Electric Easements:**\n    *   A **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is indicated by a dashed line running inside parallel to the southern property line.\n    *   A **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69 Pg. 14 Vol. 73 Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is labeled on the middle-eastern property boundary (east of Bldg. 6).\n    *   A **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** is labeled near the bottom-right (southeast) corner.\n\n**2. Analysis of Facilities against OHE/Easement Locations:**\n\n*   **Buildings (Bldg. 1 - Bldg. 8):** None of the primary building structures appear to be positioned directly under the `---OHE---` lines or within the dashed boundaries of the labeled electric easements.\n*   **Trash Enclosures:** There are no distinct masonry trash enclosures or dumpster pads plotted on this plan (the \"Trash Collection Notes\" suggest the use of curbside containers rather than a fixed enclosure structure).\n*   **Lighting Fixtures:** Specific locations for light poles are not plotted on this plan (only a detail drawing for \"Fully-Shielded Light Fixtures\" is provided in the bottom left). Therefore, conflicts cannot be determined from this sheet.\n*   **Signs:** A \"Road End Sign\" is shown on the far left side, but it appears to be located in the public right-of-way outside the primary property boundary's OHE line. No other signs are explicitly plotted within easements on the site.\n*   **Structures (Retaining Walls, Flatwork):**\n    *   *Potential Conflict (Retaining Wall):* Along the middle-eastern property boundary, there is a label for a **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69 Pg. 14 Vol. 73 Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** Directly within this area, running parallel to the property line, is a solid line representing a wall. A leader line points directly to this wall with the exact text: **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**. Based on the drawing, this structure is positioned within the labeled electric easement.\n    *   *Flatwork Intersections:* While standard flatwork is not always classified as a structural \"facility\" depending on specific local utility codes, it should be noted that the elements labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway\"** (on both the western and southern boundaries) and **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\"** (on the western boundary) physically cross directly under/over the lines marked `---OHE---` to connect to the public roadway."}]}
