{"level":30,"time":1778271785841,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014w8TvnEBw2qNi8cAmpz7pU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"ca27a08f-c387-44f8-aa3a-4d3d48b9c68a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778271785841,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ToCDv1NVn9XG9dAUYSyZ3v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The site plan doesn't mention any transmission facilities, only refers to utility providers in general. The site has only distribution-level electric services (typical for a residential development).\n\nNow I have enough information to complete my assessment. Let me finalize my findings based on all the evidence I've gathered:\n\n## Summary of Research Findings:\n\n**Site Context:**\n- Valley View Townhomes (39 units, 8 buildings)\n- 2.16 acres in MF-2 zoning\n- Overhead electric distribution line shown on landscape plan (no transmission lines mentioned)\n- Underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, meters) shown on electrical design plan\n- Existing tree canopies shown overlaying electrical plan\n\n**Landscape Documentation:**\n- **Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan)**: Shows overhead electric line (OHE), buildings, parking, and trees\n  - Trees marked with functional designations: M (mitigation), PL (parking lot), SY (street yard)\n  - NO species identification on the landscape plan itself\n  - NO mature height information on the landscape plan\n  - NO utility compatibility (UC) designation anywhere\n  - NO clearance measurements from trees to utilities\n\n- **Sheet 35 (Plant Schedule)**: Lists proposed plants\n  - Shade trees: 2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm\n  - Ornamental trees: 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, 6 Mexican Redbud\n  - Shrubs and groundcovers\n  - NO mature height information provided\n  - NO utility compatibility (UC) designation\n  - NO reference to electric utility clearances\n\n- **Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan)**: Shows underground utilities\n  - Electrical transformers, pull boxes, vaults, meters marked\n  - Underground electric lines routing throughout site\n  - Existing tree canopies shown\n  - BUT: Does NOT show overhead electric pole locations\n  - Landscape plan does NOT show underground electrical infrastructure locations\n  \nThe overhead distribution line runs along Valley View Road with no transmission easement boundaries documented. Critical gaps remain: no species or height data for trees on the landscape plan, no utility compatibility verification, no clearance distances specified between proposed plantings and the overhead line or pad-mount equipment, and no coordination shown between the landscape and electrical plans regarding equipment locations.\n\nChecking against the standards: EL-2.1 applies since overhead distribution is present, but I cannot verify tree species compatibility without external references—the plant schedule lacks UC designations. EL-2.2 doesn't apply as no transmission lines exist. For EL-2.3, I need to assess whether large trees (40+ feet mature height) fall within 25 feet of the distribution conductor, but without mature height information on either the landscape plan or plant schedule, this cannot be verified from the submitted documentation.\n\nEL-2.4 through EL-2.5 are not applicable due to the absence of transmission infrastructure. EL-2.6 requires checking tree placement relative to utility poles—the electrical plan shows pole locations, but the landscape plan doesn't correlate these positions with proposed plantings, making distance verification impossible. EL-2.7 similarly applies where pad-mounted equipment exists, but I cannot confirm clearances without both plans showing the same reference points.\n\nFor EL-2.8 and EL-2.9, underground equipment locations appear on the electrical plan while the landscape plan lacks this information entirely, preventing any assessment of tree proximity or root barrier requirements. EL-2.10 addresses the plant legend's failure to identify species.\n\nThe landscape plan legend only provides functional categories (M, PL, SY, P) rather than species identification, which fails the requirement. While a plant schedule exists on Sheet 35, the landscape plan itself—which is what the checklist references—does not include species names. For EL-2.11, trees near overhead lines lack mature height specifications, making it impossible to distinguish which ones qualify as large trees. EL-2.12 addresses clearance requirements.\n\nSince no clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the landscape plan between trees and utilities, I cannot assess whether measurements are taken from poles or conductors—this determination is N/A. Similarly, EL-2.13 cannot be evaluated because no clearance measurements exist to verify if they're measured from canopy or trunk. However, EL-2.14 passes: the overhead electric facilities and trees are both depicted on the same plan in their relative positions.\n\nFor EL-2.15, I cannot determine if trees occupy prohibited zones without knowing their species and mature heights, and no Austin Energy approvals are documented anywhere on the plans. The final assessment shows two failures (species identification and large tree differentiation with mature heights missing) and five items that cannot be verified due to missing ECM references, mature height data, and clearance measurements.\n\nFive additional items are not applicable since there are no transmission lines or easements present on the site, and no clearance measurements are shown on the plans. One item passes—trees and overhead electric service are both depicted together on the landscape plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3893,"cache_read_input_tokens":57599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3893},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"bbb1ae97-19e7-4bf0-9f78-66c45aa8e4ef"}
{"level":30,"time":1778271785842,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ToCDv1NVn9XG9dAUYSyZ3v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my research of the site plans and documents, I now have sufficient information to evaluate all checklist items for this grouping. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Key Findings from Site Plan Documentation:**\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure:**\n- Overhead electric distribution line (OHE) IS shown on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) along the southern property boundary (Valley View Road)\n- No transmission lines are present or mentioned\n- Electrical poles are indicated on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21)\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows multiple trees marked with functional designations: M (mitigation), PL (parking lot), SY (street yard)\n- Trees are shown in proximity to the overhead electric line\n- Sheet 35 (Plant Schedule) lists tree species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud, plus shrubs and groundcovers\n\n**Critical Documentation Gaps:**\n- **NO species identification** on the landscape plan legend (only functional categories M, PL, SY shown)\n- **NO mature height information** provided on either landscape plan or plant schedule\n- **NO utility compatibility (UC) designation** anywhere on the plans\n- **NO clearance measurements** from trees to overhead electric line\n- **NO clearance measurements** from trees to poles\n- **NO reference to pad-mount equipment locations** on the landscape plan\n- **NO reference to underground electric equipment locations** on the landscape plan\n- **NO root barrier specifications** on any sheet\n- **NO Austin Energy approvals** or waivers referenced\n\n**Underground Electric Infrastructure:**\n- Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, vaults, and underground lines\n- These are NOT referenced on the landscape plan where tree placements are shown\n\nNow I'll provide my final findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3893,"cache_read_input_tokens":57599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3893},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7435c0-6e4e-4832-a8a2-cd00cbe522f8","uuid":"8acb84c0-54bd-42c4-add4-d5d83873087b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778271785842,"pid":53120,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ToCDv1NVn9XG9dAUYSyZ3v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01USevHbSdby7cQLcVfBgLLs","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape near overhead electric distribution line along southern property boundary (Valley View Road)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed trees are shown on the landscape plan near the overhead electric distribution line, but the plant schedule does not identify which species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F UC designation. Utility-compatibility status cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists tree species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but provides no 'UC' (utility-compatible) designation. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows trees near overhead electric line marked only as M/PL/SY functional categories, not species.","reasoning":"The plant schedule exists but does not verify utility-compatibility status against ECM Appendix F requirements. The landscape plan does not show species identification for trees shown near utilities. Therefore, compliance with utility-compatibility requirements cannot be determined from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape near overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule does not provide mature height information for any proposed trees. Large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) cannot be identified or differentiated from the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists tree species and container sizes but contains no 'Mature Height' or 'MH' column. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows trees only with functional category labels (M/PL/SY), with no height information.","reasoning":"Without mature height specifications in the plant schedule or notation on the landscape plan, it is impossible to identify which trees are 40+ feet at maturity. Large trees cannot be distinguished from smaller species, so clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric utility poles are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) but landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show pole locations. Tree locations relative to poles cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical design plan shows overhead electric line (OHE) with poles indicated. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows proposed trees near OHE line but does not mark pole positions, making it impossible to measure the 10-foot lateral distance requirement from trees to pole centers.","reasoning":"The landscape plan lacks utility pole location references needed to verify the 10-lateral-foot clearance requirement. The pole locations from Sheet 21 are not cross-referenced or overlaid on Sheet 31 where trees are shown.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near pad-mounted electrical transformers"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted electrical transformers are marked on the electrical design plan but their locations are not shown on the landscape plan where tree placements are depicted. Clearances from trees to pad-mounts cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan identifies multiple 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations (west of Bldg. 1, 2, 8; east of Bldg. 4; south of Bldg. 7). Sheet 31 landscape plan shows proposed trees but does not reference or show transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations marked on the landscape plan, the 10-lateral-foot clearance from equipment to proposed trees cannot be measured or verified. The utility infrastructure and landscape plans are not cross-referenced.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas with underground electrical infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electrical equipment (pull boxes, vaults) is shown on the electrical plan but not referenced on the landscape plan. Clearances from proposed trees to underground equipment cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines and equipment (pull boxes, vaults). Sheet 31 landscape plan shows proposed trees but does not indicate underground equipment locations, preventing distance verification.","reasoning":"The landscape plan lacks reference to underground utility infrastructure, making it impossible to verify the 5-lateral-foot minimum clearance requirement from trees to underground equipment.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not show underground electrical equipment locations. Root barriers are not specified in any landscape notes or details. Compliance with root barrier requirements cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan notes (irrigation notes, general notes, key notes) contain no mention of root barriers. Sheet 35 plant schedule contains no root barrier specifications. Underground equipment locations are not shown on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"Two separate deficiencies combine here: (1) cannot identify trees within 20 feet of underground equipment because equipment locations are not shown on landscape plan; (2) root barrier specifications (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) are not addressed anywhere on the plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape near overhead electric distribution line and throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan legend defines tree symbols only as functional categories (M=Mitigation, PL=Parking Lot, SY=Street Yard, P=Parking Buffer Point Tree) but does not identify species. Species cannot be determined from the landscape plan where trees are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 Block 5 (Key Notes & Legend) defines symbols as: 'SY - STREET YARD TREE', 'PL - PARKING LOT TREE', 'P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE', 'M - MITIGATION TREE'. These are functional category definitions, not species. No species labels appear on the landscape plan drawing itself.","reasoning":"The landscape plan legend (the place where tree symbols should be identified) contains only functional/regulatory categories, not botanical species. Although a plant schedule exists on Sheet 35, the landscape plan itself does not provide species identification for the trees shown.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape near overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees shown on landscape plan are not marked with mature height information. Plant schedule does not provide mature heights. Large trees (40+ feet) cannot be differentiated from smaller trees to verify clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows trees marked only as M/PL/SY without height notation. Sheet 35 plant schedule lists species and container sizes but no 'Mature Height' column. Trees near overhead electric line are shown identically regardless of eventual size.","reasoning":"Mature height information is essential to identify large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) that are subject to the 25-foot distribution and 50-foot transmission clearance requirements. Without this information on either the landscape plan or plant schedule, large trees cannot be distinguished.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance measurements or dimension lines are shown on the landscape plan between trees and overhead electric lines, so the measurement methodology cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows overhead electric line (OHE) and trees in proximity, but contains no dimension lines, distance callouts, or annotations indicating clearance measurements between them.","reasoning":"This deficiency only applies when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. Since no clearance measurements are dimensioned on the landscape plan, the measurement methodology cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance measurements or dimension lines are shown on the landscape plan, so the measurement reference point (canopy vs. trunk) cannot be evaluated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan contains no dimension lines or distance callouts between trees and utility lines.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only when clearance measurements are dimensioned. Since no measurements are shown, the reference point cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape near overhead electric distribution line along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric line (OHE) and proposed trees are both shown on the landscape plan in spatial relationship, allowing clearance verification in principle.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan explicitly shows overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' along the southern property edge, and multiple trees are depicted on the same plan sheet in close proximity to this line. Both elements are visible in the same drawing with consistent scale.","reasoning":"The requirement is satisfied because both the overhead electric facilities and the proposed trees are shown on the same landscape plan, allowing a reviewer to assess their spatial relationship and identify potential clearance conflicts.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead and underground electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not identify which proposed trees are within prohibited clearance zones (species and mature heights not specified). No Austin Energy written approval is referenced. Applicability and compliance cannot be determined.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 31 and 35 contain no references to Austin Energy, no approval letters, and no species/height information to determine if trees fall within prohibited zones (15 feet for non-compatible from distribution, 25 feet for large trees from distribution, etc.).","reasoning":"Trees cannot be assessed against prohibited zones without knowing their species (to determine utility-compatibility) and mature heights (to determine if 40+ feet). Additionally, any non-compliant trees would require documented Austin Energy written approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4 Exceptions, which is not referenced anywhere on the plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines (≥60kV) are present or proposed on the site. This requirement applies only when transmission facilities are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site facts confirm only distribution-level