es indicated on plans; applicability cannot be determined)\n\n25. **EL-13.25** - 12-inch clearance from other utilities: NOT-VERIFIABLE (Utility crossing details absent from documentation)\n\n26. **EL-13.26** - Utilities not located over/under facilities: NOT-VERIFIABLE (No utility crossing analysis provided)\n\n27. **EL-13.27** - 7.5-foot clearance from overhead distribution: NOT-VERIFIABLE (Overhead line locations not shown relative to pads)\n\n28. **EL-13.28** - 15-foot radius from overhead conductors: NOT-VERIFIABLE (Overhead line positions not marked on plans)\n\n29. **EL-13.29** - 35-foot niche clearance: N/A (No niche configuration present)\n\n30. **EL-13.30** - Niche fire walls/vent Vertical clearances lack cross-sectional documentation, so I cannot verify compliance. Drainage patterns around transformer locations aren't clearly shown on the grading plan, and transformer type specifications are missing. Property line boundaries aren't annotated at pad locations, making it impossible to confirm they're entirely on private property. While one Vault Easement appears on the plans, other potential easement conflicts remain unclear. Most critically, transformer easements aren't labeled around the majority of pad locations.\n\nRouting from pads to meters shows no details confirming private property compliance. Without AE Design detail sheets or dimensional callouts on the plans, I can't verify pad dimensions match specifications. Multiple transformer pads sit within 4 feet of parking areas, yet no bollard protection is shown—this is a clear failure. Overhead line locations aren't clearly marked, preventing verification of facility conflicts. The main deficiencies center on missing transformer easement labels, absent bollard protection at parking-adjacent locations, and insufficient documentation of routing and dimensional details.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41