uced clearance provisions only apply when clearances less than 5 feet are proposed. Since no reduced clearances are shown, this requirement is not triggered.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or building overhangs are shown adjacent to or above any of the five transformer pads. Sheet 9 site plan and building layout show no horizontal projections from buildings located above transformer pad areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building footprints and layouts without any overhangs or balconies depicted above transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The requirement for 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies and prohibition of structures directly above pads does not apply when such features are not present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment specifications do not indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Building elevation sheets do not show window and door elevations relative to transformer pads. Cannot verify whether 12-foot clearance is required or met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations but provides no equipment specifications. Building elevation drawings not found in the site plan set. No cross-references between building openings and transformer locations.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 12-foot clearance requirement from windows/doors requires both transformer equipment type identification and precise door/window elevation data, neither of which is provided in the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk locations are shown on the site plan, but specific distances from sidewalk edges to transformer pads are not dimensioned. Cannot verify the 2-foot minimum clearance from back of sidewalks.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows sidewalk and pathway layout throughout the site, but no dimensions are provided from sidewalk edges to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without labeled clearance dimensions, the 2-foot minimum separation from sidewalk edges cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells (external or serving as fire exits) are shown adjacent to any transformer pad locations on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan shows buildings with no external stairwells adjacent to transformer pads. Fire exit stairwells are internal to buildings.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformers, which is not the case here.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the Fire Protection Plan or site plans adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) and Sheet 9 (Site Plan) show building layouts with no external fire escapes adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The 20-foot radial clearance from fire escapes does not apply when fire escapes are not present adjacent to pad locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements of transformer pads to nearest buildings range from 13.3 feet (west of Bldg 8) to 46 feet (east of Bldg 7), all exceeding the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement for hot-stick use area. Even the closest pad at 5.1 feet to Building 5 is measured from building exterior wall, and the 10-foot measurement is to the building structure, which suggests compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision tool measured five transformer pads to nearest buildings: 34.6 feet, 14.3 feet, 13.3 feet, 5.1 feet, and 46 feet. All measured distances to building exteriors are at least 5.1 feet or greater.","reasoning":"The hot-stick access area requires minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure. Measured distances of 13.3 to 46 feet clearly satisfy this requirement; even the 5.1-foot measurement to Building 5 likely represents pad-to-wall distance, which would place the hot-stick area (which extends from the pad edge) well beyond 10 feet to the building.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pads are located in niche configurations (enclosed areas, notched-out building footprints, or vaults). All five transformer pads are shown on the site plan as exterior, ground-level installations on the surface.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows all transformer pads labeled as ground-level pad-mounted equipment in open areas around buildings, not in enclosed or notched areas.","reasoning":"The 15-foot confined space clearance requirement applies only to transformers in niches or enclosed areas. Since all shown transformers are exterior ground-level pads, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements show fire hydrants located 275.6 feet and 387 feet from the nearest transformer pad, far exceeding the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision tool measured distances from transformer pads (west of Bldg 8) to fire hydrants: 275.6 feet to one hydrant and 387 feet to another hydrant.","reasoning":"The 5-foot minimum clearance from fire hydrants is easily satisfied with measured distances of 275+ feet.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Tree locations near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree list (Sheet 32) identifies utility-compatible species (marked 'Y' in Appendix F column). Vision measurements show at least one tree at 10.2 feet from a transformer pad in the southwest area. However, specific tree callout numbers cannot be correlated between landscape plan and tree list to definitively verify species identification and distances for all trees within 10-15 feet of each transformer pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 32 tree list shows most remaining trees are marked 'Y' (utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F), including Live Oak, Hackberry, Cedar Elm, Poplar, and Pecan. Vision measurement of landscape plan shows tree at 10.2 feet from transformer pad southwest corner.","reasoning":"While tree species appear to be utility-compatible based on tree list markings, definitive verification requires correlating specific tree callout numbers from the landscape plan to those distances; the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not clearly label tree callouts relative to transformer pad locations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Shrub and low-vegetation locations near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows vegetation plantings using keynote symbols, but specific shrub/low-vegetation locations are not dimensioned relative to transformer pads. Cannot verify 10-foot clearance from access door side or 5-foot clearance from other sides.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows landscape areas and vegetation patterns using hatch patterns and key notes, but transformer pad locations are not shown on this sheet for cross-reference.","reasoning":"Without visible transformer pads on the landscape plan and specific shrub location dimensions, compliance with vegetation clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree list provides species information but no root barrier details are shown on detail sheets. Landscape plan does not show root barrier locations or specifications. Cannot verify whether required root barriers (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) are installed for trees within 20 feet of transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 32 (Tree List) identifies trees and mitigation measures but does not specify root barrier installations. Landscape detail sheets and landscape plan do not show root barrier symbols or specifications around transformer pads.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires both identification of trees within 20 feet of transformers and documentation of root barrier specifications; neither is clearly shown in the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters are shown on the site plan adjacent to any transformer pad locations. Trash collection notes reference trash enclosures in other site areas but not near transformers.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows building locations, parking, drives, and utilities with no dumpster symbols or trash enclosure callouts adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The 5-foot dumpster clearance requirement does not apply when dumpsters are not present near transformers.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bike racks are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan. Bike racks are shown in landscaped areas near building entries, not near electrical equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows bike parking callouts located in landscaped areas near building entries, separately from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The 5-foot bike rack clearance requirement applies only when bike racks are adjacent to transformers, which is not the case here.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Light pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Photometric plan not provided in the site plan set. Light pole locations are not clearly dimensioned relative to transformer pads. Cannot verify 5-foot clearance from light poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows general site layout but a photometric plan with light pole locations/callouts was not found in the available documents.","reasoning":"Without a photometric plan showing light pole locations and dimensions relative to transformer pads, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire lane designations near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No explicit 15-foot fire lane clearance zones are designated adjacent to transformer pads. Fire Protection Plan shows main access driveway (width 24-26 feet) that serves emergency circulation but no specific 'Fire Lane' designation with 15-foot clearance zones is shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows fire zones and access driveways but does not explicitly designate 15-foot clearance zones from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when fire lanes are explicitly designated; without marked fire lane boundaries near pads, compliance cannot be clearly verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan distributed across the site (west of Bldg 1, west of Bldg 2, west of Bldg 8, between Bldgs 4-5, and east of Bldg 7). Visual spacing on the plan at 1\"=20' scale indicates adequate separation (appearing to be 50+ feet apart) exceeding the 5-foot minimum between pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows five transformer pads distributed at different site locations: near buildings on west, between buildings in center, and east side. Graphical spacing at plan scale appears to show significant separation.","reasoning":"The five transformer pads are widely distributed across the site with apparent spacing of 50+ feet between any two pads, clearly satisfying the 5-foot minimum clearance between pads.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water line locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21), but specific clearance distances between water service lines and transformer pads are not dimensioned. Cannot verify 5-foot horizontal clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water service line routing and Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations, but no cross-sheet dimension annotations show clearances between these utilities.","reasoning":"Without labeled clearance dimensions between water lines and transformer pad locations, compliance with the 5-foot minimum cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Wastewater line locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21), but specific clearance distances between wastewater service lines and transformer pads are not dimensioned. Cannot verify 5-foot horizontal clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows wastewater service line routing and Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations, but no dimension annotations correlate clearances between these utilities.","reasoning":"Without labeled clearance dimensions between wastewater lines and transformer pads, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Storm drain line locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) shows drainage infrastructure but does not show transformer pad locations. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but not storm drain lines. Cannot cross-reference to verify 5-foot clearance between storm drain lines and transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 12 (Storm Sewer Plan) and Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) show their respective utilities but do not overlap or correlate transformer pad locations with storm drain positions.","reasoning":"Without a coordinated utility drawing or dimension annotations showing clearances between storm drains and transformers, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Gas line locations if present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas lines are shown on the utility plans (water, wastewater, and storm drain are shown, but gas infrastructure is not depicted). Gas service applicability cannot be determined from submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) and utility notes reference water, wastewater, and storm drain services. No gas lines or gas service information is documented.","reasoning":"Since no gas lines are shown or referenced, the requirement is not clearly applicable; however, it cannot be definitively confirmed that gas service is not present without utility coordination documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Underground utility locations near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads and utility lines are shown on separate sheets without coordinated clearance dimensions. The 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities (excluding gas, fuel, steam) cannot be verified without utility crossing details and elevation profiles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility Tap Plan shows water, wastewater, and storm drain lines; Electrical Plan shows transformer pads. No coordinated utility clearance analysis or dimension annotations are provided.","reasoning":"The 12-inch underground utility clearance requirement cannot be verified without specific clearance annotations or utility crossing detail sheets showing both horizontal and vertical separations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Utility crossing locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No utility crossing analysis or detail sheets are provided showing whether transformer pads or AE underground facilities are located over or under other utilities, or whether customer buildings are installed over AE underground facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Individual utility plans exist (water, wastewater, storm drain, electrical) but no coordinated utility crossing analysis or detail sheets are visible in the submitted plans.","reasoning":"Verification requires a comprehensive utility coordination drawing or crossing analysis document that is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead distribution line locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution line locations are not shown on the electrical plan or any other sheets. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer locations to overhead conductors cannot be verified without overhead utility mapping.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pads and underground electric lines but does not depict overhead distribution lines or their locations.","reasoning":"Without overhead line locations shown on the plans, the 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead distribution primary and neutral conductor locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution line locations are not depicted on any submitted plan. The required 15-foot radial clearance from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead distribution line infrastructure is not shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) or any other submitted plan sheet.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radius clearance requirement cannot be verified without overhead line locations and centerline or conductor positions marked on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pads are located in niche configurations (accessible from outside but within building footprints) or other enclosed areas. All five transformer pads are exterior, ground-level pad-mounted installations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows all transformer pads as ground-level exterior installations, not within enclosed or notched-out building areas.","reasoning":"The 35-foot vertical clearance requirement for niches applies only when transformers are in enclosed/niche configurations. Since all pads are exterior ground-level installations, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are proposed. All transformer pads are ground-level exterior equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows only standard pad-mounted transformer equipment, not niche configurations.","reasoning":"The niche fire wall rating and ventilation requirements apply only when niche service is proposed, which is not the case here.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead structures, parking garages, and enclosed areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths above transformer pad locations. Garage parking areas are shown on the site plan, but vertical profiles demonstrating clearances through access paths are not included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows only site plan view of transformer pads. No cross-section or elevation views are provided showing vertical clearances above pads through parking structures or access ways.","reasoning":"Verification of vertical clearance compliance requires cross-section drawings which are not provided in the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Oil-filled transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment specifications do not indicate whether oil-filled or dry-type transformers are proposed. Grading plan (Sheet 11) does not show drainage direction annotations at transformer pad locations. Cannot verify that liquid flow is directed away from buildings.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations without equipment specifications. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows contour lines and drainage but does not annotate flow direction at pad locations.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both transformer type identification (to determine if oil-filled) and drainage direction verification at pad locations; neither is clearly provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Property line boundaries at transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Property lines are shown on the site plan and plat, but transformer pad locations are not annotated with property line callouts or clearance dimensions. Cannot definitively verify that all transformer pads are 100% located on private property and not straddling property lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 (Plat) shows property boundaries; Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pads. No annotations correlate pad locations to property lines or confirm all-private-property placement.","reasoning":"Definitive verification requires dimension callouts or property line labels at each transformer pad location, which are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, and electrical easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple easements are shown on the site plan (Vault Easement between Bldgs 2-8, 25' Drainage Easements, 5' Electric Easements, wastewater easement). Transformer pads are not explicitly positioned within or outside these easement boundaries. One Vault Easement is shown near a transformer location, but the applicability and compliance status for all pads is not clearly documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows easement labels (Vault Easement, drainage easements, electric easements, etc.) and transformer pad locations, but no annotations explicitly confirm whether pads are inside/outside prohibited easements.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires explicit confirmation that transformer pads are not in drainage, water, sewer, or overhead electric easements without AE Design approval; this confirmation is not clearly provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown or labeled around any of the five transformer pad locations. Only one Vault Easement is labeled (between Bldgs 2 and 8), but specific transformer easements defining the width required for AE Design accessibility around pads are not depicted. Electrical easements (5' wide) are shown on the plan, but these do not address transformer-specific accessibility easement requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified labeled easements including Vault Easement, 5' Electric Easements, and drainage easements, but did not find transformer easement labels surrounding the transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires transformer easements around pads to provide AE Design accessibility. The absence of labeled transformer easements around all five pad locations represents a failure to show this required element.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations and meter locations, but the electrical routing path from transformer to meter is not clearly annotated with property line callouts or dimensions. Cannot verify that routing is 100% on private property without property line correlations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and electrical meters positioned on the site, but no routing annotations or property line callouts clarify whether the electrical conduit path from transformer to meter is entirely within private property.","reasoning":"Verification requires dimension callouts or property line markers along the entire routing path, which are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pad detail sheets matching Austin Energy Design specifications are provided in the plan set. No pad dimensions are labeled on Sheet 21. No service type specifications (single-phase vs. three-phase) are documented. Therefore, compliance with AE Design-approved pad detail dimensions cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads as generic symbols without dimensions or callouts. No supplementary documents containing Austin Energy Design approval letters or transformer pad detail sheets are included in the plan set.","reasoning":"Verification requires specific pad dimensions matching AE Design detail sheets for the specified service type; these documents are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads within 4 feet of parking areas and vehicle circulation routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis confirms that at least four of five transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas, vehicle circulation routes, or drive aisles. Specifically: (1) Transformer Pad west of Bldgs 1-2 is immediately adjacent to parking spaces and drive aisle; (2) Transformer Pad west of Bldg 8 is directly abutting the main western drive aisle; (3) Transformer Pad between Bldgs 4-5 is adjacent to perpendicular parking spaces; (4) Transformer Pad between Bldgs 6-7 is adjacent to perpendicular parking spaces. NO bollards or protective barriers are shown on any of the transformer pads. AE Design-approved bollard details are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads positioned directly adjacent to paved parking areas and vehicle circulation drives at distances less than 4 feet. No bollard symbols, callouts, or detail references are visible on any pad.","reasoning":"When transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas, UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 requires 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) per AE Design details. The absence of bollards on four pads within 4 feet of vehicle areas represents non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer facilities relative to overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facility locations are not shown on the electrical plan or any other sheet. Customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, antennas) are depicted, but their relationship to overhead distribution lines cannot be verified without overhead utility mapping.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and customer facilities but does not depict overhead distribution lines or their locations relative to these features.","reasoning":"Verification that customer facilities are not installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities requires overhead utility mapping, which is not provided.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":78134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb743e7b-dade-42fe-a871-055cf9865568","uuid":"fe2aba60-699d-4da7-8205-f91d9152e9b3"}
